Emeka and Femi are partners with capitals of ₦3,000,000 and ₦2,000,000 respectively. On 1 January 2025 their current account balances were: Emeka ₦150,000 (credit) and Femi ₦40,000 (debit). The partnership agreement provides:
(i) interest on capital at 10% per annum;
(ii) Femi to receive a salary of ₦360,000 per annum;
(iii) interest on drawings: Emeka ₦18,000, Femi ₦12,000;
(iv) residual profits shared in the ratio 3 : 2.
Net profit for 2025 was ₦1,650,000. Drawings were Emeka ₦600,000 and Femi ₦450,000.
Prepare:
(a) the profit and loss appropriation account; [8 marks]
(b) the partners' current accounts. [7 marks]

Adamawa Foods Plc had the following balances on 1 January 2025: ordinary share capital (5,000,000 shares of ₦1 each, fully paid) ₦5,000,000; 10% preference share capital (1,000,000 shares of ₦1 each) ₦1,000,000; share premium ₦500,000; general reserve ₦400,000; retained earnings ₦650,000; 12% debentures ₦2,000,000.
For the year ended 31 December 2025:
(i) profit before debenture interest and tax was ₦2,840,000;
(ii) income tax is 30% of profit before tax;
(iii) ₦300,000 is to be transferred to general reserve;
(iv) the preference dividend and an ordinary dividend of 10% were paid during the year.
Prepare:
(a) an extract of the income statement from profit before interest and tax to profit after tax; [4 marks]
(b) a statement of retained earnings for the year; [6 marks]
(c) the equity section of the statement of financial position at 31 December 2025. [5 marks]
